WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.665
- [Narrator] Meet streptococcus mutans.

00:00:02.665 --> 00:00:04.231
- Hey. My friends call me Strep.

00:00:04.231 --> 00:00:08.223
- [Narrator] He's a bacterium
and a bit of a slob.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.740
But this isn't just any mess.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.110
It's what's on your teeth.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:18.980
You see, strep and all his
roommates live inside your mouth.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:22.325
Feeding off of the sugar
and protein in your food.

00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:26.000
When they're done, they
excrete a slimy substance

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.284
all over your pearly whites.

00:00:28.284 --> 00:00:33.284
The end result is a bacteria
ridden pigsty called biofilm.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.342
Now, a little biofilm
isn't gonna hurt you.

00:00:37.342 --> 00:00:40.090
It's only when you stop brushing it away

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.152
that things can get ugly.

00:00:42.152 --> 00:00:45.040
And not only for your teeth.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.410
It just so happens that
strep and his friends

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.793
are a downright threat to your life.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.210
Nearly half of Americans don't
brush their teeth enough.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.620
And when food builds up in
those nooks and crannies,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.020
you're inviting a host
of bacteria to the party.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.220
Including your gumline.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.910
Which irritate and inflame your gums

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:12.400
causing tenderness and bleeding.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.500
But that's just the start.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.660
Soon enough, that infection
will trigger your immune system

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:22.240
which sends fighter cells
to battle the bacteria.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.890
This creates a hostile
environment for the bacteria.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:29.900
Which is what you want but
it can also damage the cells

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.915
in nearby tissue and bone.

00:01:31.915 --> 00:01:35.950
Six months to years later
that tissue and bone

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.423
will eventually die.

00:01:37.423 --> 00:01:41.200
At this point, you don't
have gingivitis anymore.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.930
You have something much worse:

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:46.210
periodontal disease.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:50.320
No more tissue and bone means
no more structural support.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.200
So, your gums separate from
your teeth forming pockets

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.950
that quickly become extra space
for strep and his friends.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.060
Which further infects your gums

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.330
causing your teeth to fall out.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.656
Now, you may think this
could never happen to you

00:02:05.656 --> 00:02:10.656
but about 10% of Americans
between ages 50-64

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:16.376
have lost not one, not two,
but all of their teeth.

00:02:16.376 --> 00:02:20.590
And to make matters worse,
strep and his buddies may enter

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:23.170
your blood stream where
they'll wreak havoc

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.784
on your organs too.

00:02:24.784 --> 00:02:29.500
For example, in one study,
people with periodontal disease

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:33.360
were four and a half times
more likely to have chronic

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.900
kidney disease than
people with healthy gums.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.870
And another study found that people

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:42.260
in a retirement community who
didn't brush their teeth daily

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.890
had up to 65% greater risk of dementia.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.490
Last but not least,

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:52.252
there's an increased risk of
developing certain cancers.

00:02:52.252 --> 00:02:55.910
To be fair, these risks
can also be the result

00:02:55.910 --> 00:03:00.740
of poor hygiene in general
but the message remains clear.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.330
Brush your teeth.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.803
It's worth the extra four minutes a day.

